Generally, you've got to keep track along the way. You can find out
for sure by drinking a potion of enlightenment or zapping a wand of
enlightenment (or sometimes by sitting on a throne but you probably
haven't seen one of those yet).

Some of these intrinsics are gained by eating monsters, some are by
getting items. You can see the "eating corpses for food and
intrinsics" spoiler if you want to know which monsters to eat and
which ones to avoid. There are certain keywords that show up after you
eat a corpse that tell you if you've gained an intrinsic. "You Feel
Healthy." is the one you see after gaining poison resistance, for
example.

http://www.geocities.com/dcorbett42/nethack/corpse.htm

Magic resistance, magic cancellation, and reflection are only gained
by wearing items. Magic resistance is generally gained by wearing a
cloak of magic resistance, or gray dragon scale mail, or by wishing
for an artifact that grants it. Magic cancellation is a property of
some armor (that can be found on the armor spoiler), and generally if
you wear a cloak of some kind you're okay. Some are better than
others, consult the armor spoiler for details. Reflection is gained by
wearing an amulet or wearing a shield of reflection. There is a 50%
chance that the top level in sokoban has an amulet of reflection (and
50% chance that it's a bag of holding)

